==================================================
PART 15 — RELATED TOPICS
==================================================

Topic pages should show related topics when real relationships exist.

Examples:

Decision Tree
→ Random Forest
→ SVM
→ Logistic Regression

BUT:

Do not invent relationships automatically just because topics belong to the same course.

Prefer:

- explicit relatedTopics metadata
- same subject
- same unit

Use sensible fallback logic only if already supported.

Do not create dozens of low-value links.

==================================================
PART 16 — ORPHAN PAGE DETECTION
==================================================

Create a development-time check or script if practical.

Identify topic pages that have:

- no parent subject link
- no incoming internal link
- invalid related-topic links
- missing breadcrumb path

Every public topic should be reachable through:

Home
→ Notes
→ Course
→ Branch
→ Subject
→ Topic

==================================================
PART 17 — INTERNAL LINK TEXT
==================================================

Avoid generic anchor text such as:

"Click here"

"Read more"

"Learn more"

Prefer descriptive anchor text:

"Decision Tree in Machine Learning"

"Machine Learning Notes"

"Linear Regression"

"SVM in Machine Learning"

This helps both users and search engines understand the destination.

==================================================
PART 18 — IMAGE SEO
==================================================

Inspect existing images.

Every meaningful educational image should have:

- descriptive alt text
- appropriate dimensions
- responsive rendering

Do not keyword stuff alt text.

Decorative images should use appropriate empty alt where applicable.

Do not invent image descriptions when the image meaning is unknown.

==================================================
PART 19 — INTERNAL SEARCH PARAMETERS
==================================================

If the website currently has query parameters such as:

?q=
?search=
?utm_source=

do not allow tracking parameters to create canonical duplicates.

Do not index search-result pages unless there is a deliberate SEO strategy for them.

Do not implement the Search feature in this phase.

==================================================
PART 20 — 404 / INVALID ROUTES
==================================================

Verify invalid topic URLs return an appropriate 404/not-found response.

Do not render a normal topic page for:

undefined

null

missing slug

invalid course

invalid branch

invalid subject

invalid topic

Avoid soft-404 pages.

